2. thoughdump
    - Renderservice should not have anything to do with UI render. Renderservice should be the 'make prompts for LLM' service.
        - it should receive the promptctx thing from kb (data) service via the engine, and push it to clipboard via dedicated port
    - TUIService encapsulates incoming and outcoming communication with the user. the exit messages the engine uses should originate from here.

Backlog tail, Selected item/items:

let us eliminate this hotprompt exception thing. we can just have the service return the prompt, encapsulating the business of returning a normal or hot prompt.
let us also take the opportunity the to declare a proper set of Result type objects. the engine will pass the command it gets from io service to the kb service, getting a result object back which it investigates the type of (i think perhaps there are only two types? the ones which need get passed to renderservice, and the ones which are passed to io on the next loop)

